Validator logic (codepoint-based):

```java
public final class BidiIsolateValidator {
    public static final int MAX_NESTING = 4;
    // returns -1 if valid, else offending codepoint index
    public static int validate(String text) {
        Deque<Integer> stack = new ArrayDeque<>(); // indices of isolate starts
        int[] i = {0};
        int len = text.length();
        int cpIndex = 0;
        for (int offset = 0; offset < len; ) {
            int cp = text.codePointAt(offset);
            if (cp >= 0x202A && cp <= 0x202E) return cpIndex;
            if (cp == 0x2066 || cp == 0x2067 || cp == 0x2068) {
                if (stack.size() >= MAX_NESTING) return cpIndex;
                stack.push(cpIndex);
            } else if (cp == 0x2069) {
                if (stack.isEmpty()) return cpIndex;
                stack.pop();
            }
            offset += Character.charCount(cp);
            cpIndex++;
        }
        if (!stack.isEmpty()) return stack.peekLast(); // earliest unclosed start? stack is LIFO; bottom is earliest
        return -1;
    }
}
```

ArrayDeque: push adds to head. Bottom of stack = last element = peekLast(). The earliest unclosed start is at the bottom. Report that. Fine.

